# Build context for api/Dockerfile.gpu is the project root (context: ..).
# Without this file, `docker compose build` sends the entire repo —
# .git history, sample/result images, docs — to the Docker daemon on
# every build, which slows builds and needlessly increases the chance of
# a build being interrupted by a slow/flaky transfer. None of this is
# referenced by `COPY api/ .`, so it is safe to exclude.

.git
.github
.claude

# Model weights are volume-mounted at runtime (../ml:/app/ml), never
# copied into the image — excluding them keeps large checkpoint files
# out of the build context entirely.
ml/checkpoints/
ml/data/
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# Sample/result images and docs at the repo root — not used by the image.
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.pdf

# Runtime/dev artifacts never needed inside the image.
storage/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.*
